{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"id\":\"structural_monotony\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The annotator's conclusion is plausible, but this is a whole-document judgment and they supplied no comparative evidence across sections. The document does show distinct section functions that would need to be cited to support the call.\",\"evidence\":[\"The drafting group has completed the revised core terminology and incorporated the comments accepted during the June review.\",\"Two issues remain unresolved.\",\"Over the next two weeks, we need decisions on:\",\"Decision papers will be circulated by 7 August.\"]},{\"id\":\"tonal_uniformity\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The text does appear to maintain one formal project-update register, but the annotator gave no evidence from multiple parts of the document for this whole-text claim.\",\"evidence\":[\"Here is this week’s status update for the interoperability standards project.\",\"Two issues remain unresolved.\",\"Please send material changes or missing risks to me by 5 August so they can be included.\"]},{\"id\":\"faux_specificity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document does not rely on fake lived-detail filler; its details are operational and genuinely specific to project status, dates, counts, and decisions.\",\"evidence\":[\"validated 31 of the 36 required scenarios\",\"three implementation partners\",\"The steering meeting on 12 August\"]},{\"id\":\"neutrality_collapse\",\"verdict\":\"insufficient_evidence\",\"rationale\":\"The annotator's answer is plausible because the memo reports concrete unresolved issues and requested decisions rather than flattening everything into both-sides framing, but they supplied no evidence for that document-level judgment.\",\"evidence\":[\"Two issues remain unresolved.\",\"we need decisions on:\",\"The steering meeting on 12 August will be used to settle the four points above\"]},{\"id\":\"even_jargon_distribution\",\"verdict\":\"misclassified\",\"rationale\":\"The clear/no-flag status is reasonable, but the selected category is not. The jargon is not clumped into one expert-heavy subsection; it is distributed naturally throughout the update because the whole memo is a technical project-status note.\",\"evidence\":[\"interoperability standards project\",\"revised core terminology\",\"The conformance examples are now aligned with draft 0.8\",\"the identifier-retention requirement\",\"normative text or implementation guidance\",\"external-review timetable\"]},{\"id\":\"forced_synesthesia\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The prose is literal and administrative. There are no cross-sensory metaphors to flag.\",\"evidence\":[\"The data group found licensing restrictions in the proposed source and is assessing two alternatives.\",\"those scenarios cannot be completed.\"]},{\"id\":\"generic_metaphors\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document uses straightforward project-management language rather than metaphorical framing.\",\"evidence\":[\"Two issues remain unresolved.\",\"minimum pass threshold for the September trial\"]},{\"id\":\"referential_clarity\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Pronouns and definite descriptions are recoverable from nearby antecedents, and there is no excessive vague 'the + noun' cadence that obscures reference.\",\"evidence\":[\"that both teams support\",\"Until that choice is made, those scenarios cannot be completed.\",\"the four points above\"]},{\"id\":\"formulaic_parallelism\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The list and sentence structures are functional rather than sloganized; the parallel form carries substantive distinctions instead of substituting for content.\",\"evidence\":[\"- the identifier-retention rule and whether it belongs in the normative text or implementation guidance;\",\"- the replacement reference dataset;\",\"- the minimum pass threshold for the September trial;\",\"- whether draft 0.9 can proceed to external review with known limitations documented.\"]},{\"id\":\"semantic_redundancy\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document does not repeat nearby information gratuitously; later references compress earlier material rather than restating it at length.\",\"evidence\":[\"Two issues remain unresolved.\",\"the four points above\"]},{\"id\":\"underspecified_language\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The memo is specific enough for its genre. It names the relevant actions, counts, dates, and decision points rather than leaning on empty evaluative modifiers.\",\"evidence\":[\"validated 31 of the 36 required scenarios\",\"assessing two alternatives\",\"minimum pass threshold for the September trial\"]},{\"id\":\"context_leakage\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"Nothing here reads like a reply to an absent chat comment or critique. The requests and explanations are self-contained within the update.\",\"evidence\":[\"Please send material changes or missing risks to me by 5 August so they can be included.\",\"The steering meeting on 12 August will be used to settle the four points above\"]},{\"id\":\"performed_candour\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The note does not use sincerity markers such as 'honestly' or 'frankly' to perform authenticity.\",\"evidence\":[\"Here is this week’s status update for the interoperability standards project.\",\"Thanks,\"]},{\"id\":\"vacuous_connection\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The connectors state real temporal, causal, and contrastive relationships; they do not gesture at logic without supplying it.\",\"evidence\":[\"but we do not yet have language that both teams support.\",\"Until that choice is made, those scenarios cannot be completed.\",\"so they can be included.\"]},{\"id\":\"genre_specific\",\"verdict\":\"supported\",\"rationale\":\"The document is not academic, student essay, poetry, fiction, journalism, or marketing email. 'Default' is the right genre bucket, and no genre-specific watchlist findings apply.\",\"evidence\":[\"Subject: Standards project update: progress, open issues, and August decisions\",\"Hi team,\",\"Thanks,\",\"Rina\"]}]}"}}
